{"id":"word:hebrew:H7993","type":"word","title":"שָׁלַךְ","subtitle":"H7993 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to throw out, down or away (literally or figuratively)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׁלַךְ (H7993) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 125 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׁלַךְ (shâlak) means to throw out, down or away (literally or figuratively) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 13 24."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׁלַךְ","transliteration":"shâlak","pronunciation":"shaw-lak","strong":"H7993","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7993","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["מֻשְׁלֶ֣כֶת","וַ/יַּשְׁלֵ֥ךְ","וַ/יַּשְׁלֵךְ֙","וַ/יַּשְׁלֵ֤ךְ","הִשְׁלִ֥יךְ"],"morphs":[["HC/Vhw3ms",16],["HC/Vhw3mp",12],["HVhp3ms",6],["HVhi1cs",5],["HVHsfsa",4],["HVhp3cp",4],["HVhv2ms/Sp3ms",4],["HVhp2ms",3],["HC/Vhw3ms/Sp3ms",3],["HVhv2mp",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to throw out, down or away (literally or figuratively)","usage":"adventure, cast (away, down, forth, off, out), hurl, pluck, throw.","full":"H7993. shalak [ שָׁלַךְ ] 125 verb Hiph`il 112 throw, fling, cast (Phoenician שלד in compare proper name, meaning dubious; Arabic is travel (or cause to travel ) along a road, cause to enter ); — Perfect 3masculine singular הִשְׁלִיךְ Amos 8:3 +; 2 masculine singular suffix consecutive וְהִשְׁלַכְּתּוֺ Jer 51:63 ; 2 feminine plural consecutive וְהִשְׁלַכְתֶּ֫נָה Amos 4:3 , etc.; Imperfect יַשְׁלִיךְ Isa 2:20 , וַיַּשְׁלֵךְ Judg 9:17 +, etc.; Imperative masculine singular הַשְׁלֵךְ Exod 7:9 ; Psa 55:23 , feminine singular הַשְׁלִיכִי Jer 7:29 , etc.; Infinitive absolute הַשְׁלֵךְ 22:19 ; 36:23 ; construct הַשְׁלִיךְ Eccl 3:5-6 , etc.; Participle מֵשְׁלְיךְ Micah 2:5 ; Psa 147:17 , etc.; &#8212; 1 usually human subject, throw, cast: a. accusative of thing, with many preposition: e.g. אָל location 2Kin 23:12 ; Ezek 5:4 ; Zech 5:8 (twice in verse) +, also (accusative of thing omitted) Exod 15:25 (J), Num 19:6 (P) +; ב loc, Exod 32:24 (E), Ezek 7:19 +; rarely ל location 2Chr 30:14 and (accusative omitted) 24:10 ; עַל location 2Kin 23:6 , ָ ה locative Exod 4:3 (twice in verse), שָׁ֫מָּה Judg 8:25 ; 2Kin 6:6 (accusative omitted), etc.; especially of casting dead bodies, אֶל location Josh 8:29 (J), 10:27 (J), + 3 t., ב location Amos 8:3 ; 2Kin 9:25-26 ,. 13:21 , לְ מֵהָֽלְאָה Jer 22:19 ; accusative of thing + אֶל person 1Kin 19:19 ; 2Sam 20:22 (accusative omitted); accusative of thing with עַל person Nahum 3:6 ; Judg 9:53 ; 2Sam 11:21 ( + מֵעַל ), etc.; accusative of thing + מִיָּד Exod 32:19 (E), compare Deut 9:17 ( מֵעַל ); + ל of animal Exod 22:30 (E), Isa 2:20 , etc. b. with accusative of person , אֶל of pit Gen 37:22 (E), Jer 38:6 , 9 , ב of pit Gen 37:20 (E), with ה locative 37:24 (E; pit), Exod 1:22 (J), compare Amos 4:3 (si vera lectio); תַּחַת location Gen 21:15 (E); accusative ׳י , figurative, with גַוֶּךָ֑ אַחֲרֵי 1Kin 14:9 (of apostasy), Ezek 23:35 , so ׳י s law Neh 9:26 , words ( אַחֲרֵי person reflexive) Psa 50:17 . c. throw away , accusative of thing Judg 15:17 ( מִיָּדוֺ ), 2Kin 7:15 ; Ezek 20:7-8 , Psa 2:3 ( מִן reflexive), Eccl 3:5 (opposed to = כָּנַס ); accusative omitted Jer 7:29 ; Joel 1:7 (of locusts); absolute Eccl 3:6 (opposed to שָׁמַר ); accusative of transgression Ezek 18:31 (figurative; מֵעַל reflexive). d. cast off, shed , blossom (like flower) Job 15:33 . e. cast down (late), subject goat, accusative ram, Dan 8:7 ( אַ֫רְצָה ) little horn, accusative אֱמֶת 8:12 ( id. ); accusative of person (literal) 2Chr 25:12 ( מִן local), Job 18:7 his (own) counsel felleth him ; so probably Jer 9:18 they have overthrown our dwellings (Du reads Hoph`al). f. figurative, Psa 55:23 cast ׳עליֿ thy lot. 2 ׳י subject: a. cast , accusative of thing, + עַל person Josh 10:11 (E), Job 27:22 (accusative of thing omitted); sandal upon Edom Psa 60:10 = 108:10 (sign of possession); ice (no preposition) 147:17 . b. accusative of person + ב location 2Kin 2:16 (subject י ׳רוּחַ ), Neh 9:11 ; Jonah 2:4 ( + accusative of location); + אַ֫רְצָה Ezek 28:17 (figurative); אֶל location (of exile) Deut 29:27 ; especially of ׳י s rejecting men, accusative of person + מָּנָיו מֵעַל 2Kin 13:23 ; 24:20 , compare 17:20 ; Jer 7:15 (twice in verse); 52:3 , also Psa 51:13 and (without מִן ) 71:9 ; casting sins (accusative) גֵּוְךָ אַחֲרֵי Isa 38:17 , ב location Micah 7:19 . c. cast down , honour of Israel + accusative of location, מִן local, Lam 2:1 ; accusative of person Psa 102:11 (opposed to נָשָׂא ). 3 phrases: גּוֺרָל הִשׁי Josh 18:8 , 10 (R D ) cast lots ל in behalf of ; ׳מַשׁ בְגוֺרָל חֶבֶל Micah 2:5 (see גּוֺרָל 3 , I. חֶבֶל 2 ); מַשׁ חַכָּה ׳בַּיְאוֺר Isa 19:8 i.e. fishermen; מִנֶּגֶד נַפְשׁוֺ וַיַּשְׁלֵח Judg 9:17 , see נֶגֶד 2c ; אַשׁ ׳מִשּׁנָּיו טָ֑רֶף Job 29:17 out of his teeth I cast the prey. Hoph`al Perfect 3masculine singular הֻשְׁלַח Dan 8:11 ; 2 masculine singular הָשְׁלַכְתָּ Isa 14:19 , etc.; Imperfect 2feminine singular וַתֻּשְׁלְכִי Ezek 16:5 ; 3 masculine plural יֻשְׁלָ֑כוּ Isa 34:3 ; Participle מֻשְׁלָח 2Sam 20:21 , etc.; &#8212; 1 be thrown, cast , accusative of head, אֶל person + בְּעַד of wall 2Sam 20:21 ; carcass, ב location 1Kin 13:24-25 , 28 ; Jer 14:16 ; לַחֹרֶב 36:30 . 2 be cast forth, out , absolute of dead Isa 34:3 ; מִן of grave 14:19 ; הַשָּׁדֶה אֶלמְּֿנֵי Ezek 16:5 (Jerusalem personified as infant); עַלהָֿאָרֶץ Jer 22:28 (of exile). 3 be cast down , לָאָרֶץ Ezek 19:12 (Israel, figurative of vine); absolute of sanctuary Dan 8:11 . 4 metaphor , be cast , על of ׳י Psa 22:11 (i.e. on his protection).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 13 24","keyReferences":["1Kgs 13 24","1Kgs 13 25","1Kgs 13 28","1Kgs 14 9","1Kgs 19 19","2Chr 7 20","2Chr 24 10","2Chr 25 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":125,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 13 2